  "body": "**Motivation**\n\nThe builder services are merged but not connected, so a running builder only observes. This wires them into a bidding and reveal loop and connects the builder to an execution client.\n\n**Description**\n\nMinimal changes ported from existing variants of wiring.\n\nAdditions:\n- Bidder: on `payload_attributes`, builds a payload for the next slot, retrieves it at `--bidding.deadlineBps` (default 95%), prices it with `ProportionalBidPolicy` and publishes the bid\n- Revealer: publishes the envelope once a block selecting one of our bids is imported, unless it arrived after `--reveal.cutoffBps`\n- BidLedger: won bids settle three epochs after their slot\n- CLI: `--execution.*`, `--jwtSecret`, `--bidding.*`, `--reveal.cutoffBps`; the EL connection goes through `initializeExecutionEngine`\n- Kurtosis devnet config and nightly smoke test updated to run with an EL and assert bids, wins and reveals\n\nRelates to #10234, #10247, #10259, which contain several improvements over this, can be shipped as follow-ups.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nico Flaig <nflaig@protonmail.com>",
